# Animate Dead gives the Ornithopter -1/-0, so its power is -1: it deals 0 damage, not a negative amount, and is still sacrificed. Turn 3: Bot1 bolts its own
# Ornithopter (it dies), returns it with Animate Dead (-1/2), then Burn Together has it "deal damage" to Bot2 (life stays 20) and sacrifices it. Two creatures
# died under Bot1's control (the bolted card and the returned one), so the Sell-Sword cast afterwards from exile enters with two counters.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Swamp
Black Lotus
Ornithopter
Animate Dead
Lightning Bolt
Callous Sell-Sword
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Animate Dead.Cast(Ornithopter; Spend: B)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Callous Sell-Sword.Cast(Ability: Burn Together)
Bot1.Target(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = -1
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 20
? Exile = Callous Sell-Sword
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Exile.Callous Sell-Sword.Cast

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Callous Sell-Sword.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
